WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:13.698
Hi! We can say the cat chased the mouse, or the mouse was chased by the cat. English has both: the active voice and the passive voice. Let's learn how to change between them.

2
00:00:13.848 --> 00:00:19.122
In the active voice, the doer comes first. The cat chased the mouse.

3
00:00:19.272 --> 00:00:25.986
In the passive voice, the thing receiving the action comes first. The mouse was chased by the cat.

4
00:00:26.136 --> 00:00:34.146
The passive formula: a form of be, plus the past participle, and you can add by and the doer.

5
00:00:34.296 --> 00:00:41.874
The tense of be follows the original verb. Present: Ali cleans the room becomes The room is cleaned by Ali.

6
00:00:42.024 --> 00:00:45.330
Past: cleaned becomes was cleaned.

7
00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:49.578
Present perfect: has cleaned becomes has been cleaned.

8
00:00:49.728 --> 00:00:54.378
Future: will clean becomes will be cleaned.

9
00:00:54.528 --> 00:01:02.298
First, be must agree with the new subject. The cakes were baked by Mum. Cakes is plural, so we use were.

10
00:01:02.448 --> 00:01:10.290
Second, if we don't know who did it, we can leave out by. My bicycle was stolen. We don't know who stole it.

11
00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:19.578
Third, always use the past participle: written, eaten, taken, not wrote, ate, took.

12
00:01:19.728 --> 00:01:24.210
Watch out! The letter was wrote by my sister is wrong!

13
00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:31.506
The passive needs the past participle. The past tense of write is wrote, but the past participle is written.

14
00:01:31.656 --> 00:01:36.666
So we say: The letter was written by my sister.

15
00:01:36.816 --> 00:01:48.570
Your turn! The chef cooks the meal. In the passive: The meal ___ by the chef. What goes in? Pause and think.

16
00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:53.682
The answer is is cooked. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:53.832 --> 00:02:04.842
Another one! The boys broke the window. In the passive: The window ___ by the boys. Pause and think.

18
00:02:04.992 --> 00:02:13.194
The answer is was broken: was for the past, plus the past participle broken. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:13.344 --> 00:02:23.106
Try this one! The letters ___ yesterday, using deliver in the passive. Pause and think.

20
00:02:23.256 --> 00:02:32.898
The answer is were delivered. Yesterday tells us it's the past, and letters is plural, so we use were. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:33.048 --> 00:02:43.338
And another! Mum will bake a cake. In the passive: A cake ___ by Mum. Pause and think.

22
00:02:43.488 --> 00:02:54.234
The answer is will be baked. The original uses will, so the passive uses will be, plus the past participle baked. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:54.384 --> 00:03:04.146
Last one! The flowers ___ every morning, using water in the passive. Pause and think.

24
00:03:04.296 --> 00:03:11.730
The answer is are watered. Flowers is plural, so we use are. Did you get it right?

25
00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:23.490
Remember: the passive is be plus the past participle. Be keeps the tense of the original verb and agrees with the new subject. If the doer is unknown, you can leave out by.

26
00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:28.050
Try turning a sentence into the passive!

